Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:16:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 49/70] data: a text stays a string, and a colour property's "1
 1 1" is white
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two parse faults that made text vanish:
- A text object's text went through the generic value parser, which reads a string of 2-4
  space-separated words as a vector: "Sinner #8", "HHH HHH HHH", "ART MADE BY @Minau_" became a
  zero vec2/3/4 and laid out as nothing (with the old renderer too). JsonExtensions::text keeps a
  string a string (UserSettingParser/DynamicValueParser expectString); parseText uses it.
- WE's colour picker stores 0..1 floats and writes whole ones without a point ("1 1 1", "1 0 0").
  ColorBuilder read any point-less colour as 0..255, so the 117 colour user properties of the owner's
  96 scenes written that way (none has a component above 1) came out black or near it — e.g.
  2134765860's clock bound to `clock1` = "1 1 1" drew at 1/255. Colour properties now parse with
  ColorBuilder::parseProperty (whole numbers 0/1 are 0..1; a component above 1 still means 0..255).
  Object and particle colours keep the old reading (particle colorrandom writes 0..255).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B4 (text present at all)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
